# A.I.N.D.Y. Apps Monolith — Environment Variable Reference
#
# This repo is a plugin layer on top of aindy-runtime. The runtime reads its
# env from AINDY/.env inside the installed package (or from the path set by
# AINDY_ENV_FILE). For local dev against a sibling checkout, the simplest
# approach is to set AINDY_ENV_FILE to point at a .env in this repo root:
#
#   export AINDY_ENV_FILE=$(pwd)/.env
#   aindy-runtime serve   # reads .env from this directory
#
# For the full env var reference (Redis, event bus, quotas, etc.) see:
#   ../aindy-runtime/AINDY/.env.example
#
# This file documents only the vars you must set for the monolith to boot.
# DO NOT commit .env to version control.


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Group 1 — Required for any boot
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

DATABASE_URL=
# Required. PostgreSQL connection URI.
#   postgresql://aindy:aindy@localhost:5432/aindy   (local dev)
#   postgresql://aindy:aindy@postgres:5432/aindy    (Docker Compose)
# SQLite (sqlite://) is accepted only for unit tests — set AINDY_ALLOW_SQLITE=1.

SECRET_KEY=REPLACE_THIS_with_a_32_char_hex_string
# Required. JWT signing key — minimum 32 characters outside test/dev.
# Generate: python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"

OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Required for memory embeddings and LLM calls.
# Development: empty logs a warning but the server still boots.
# Production: runtime refuses to boot if unset or a known placeholder.

PERMISSION_SECRET=REPLACE_THIS_with_a_32_char_hex_string
# Required. App-layer permission signing key — keep separate from SECRET_KEY.
# Generate: python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Group 2 — Boot mode & plugin manifest
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# AINDY_BOOT_MODE=app-profile
# REQUIRED to load the 16 domain apps when serving. `aindy-runtime serve`
# setdefaults this to `runtime-only` (a platform-only profile that loads ZERO
# apps — no /apps/* routes, no agent planner), so you MUST set `app-profile`
# to boot the domains. docker-compose.prod.yml already defaults it to
# app-profile for the api service; set it here only for a bare (non-compose)
# `aindy-runtime serve`. Setting AINDY_APP_PLUGIN_MANIFEST alone is NOT enough —
# the manifest is only consulted once the profile is non-platform-only.

# AINDY_APP_PLUGIN_MANIFEST=./aindy_plugins.json
# Path to the app plugin manifest. Defaults to ./aindy_plugins.json relative
# to the working directory. Only set this if running aindy-runtime serve from
# a directory other than this repo root. Requires AINDY_BOOT_MODE=app-profile
# (above) to take effect.


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Group 3 — Optional / commonly overridden
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:5173
# Comma-separated CORS origins. Add your frontend dev server origin here.
# Production: replace with your actual deployment origin(s).

DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# Optional. Only needed if workflows route LLM calls to DeepSeek.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional for a default boot; REQUIRED to run the Claude agent planner
# (AINDY_AGENT_PLANNER_BACKEND=anthropic_chat — see Group 3 below). Also used by
# any domain that routes LLM calls to Claude. Leave blank to run on the default
# runtime_local planner. docker-compose.prod.yml already plumbs this into the api
# service; set it in your deploy .env when you enable the Claude planner.

AINDY_API_KEY=
# Optional. Bearer token for machine-to-machine calls to this runtime's API.

# MONGO_URL=mongodb://localhost:27017
# Required only if social layer or memory backends use Mongo.
# Leave unset to run without Mongo (MONGO_REQUIRED defaults to false).

# MONGO_DB_NAME=aindy_social_layer
# Mongo database name used by the social layer (posts, profiles, comments,
# metrics history) and Mongo-backed services. Defaults to "aindy_default" if
# unset. ALL social-layer code resolves the database from this single var, so
# the value only has to be consistent — but set it explicitly to match your
# deployment (production uses "aindy_social_layer").

# SOCIAL_FEED_BRIDGE_ORIGINS=system
# Comma-separated allowlist of bridge-event `origin` values surfaced in the
# social feed's `events` channel. Defaults to "system". Blank/unset-to-blank
# surfaces nothing (safe default). Widen once you know which origins are
# system/public (e.g. "system,scheduler").

# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0
# Required for distributed execution mode, event bus, and cache.
# Thread mode (the default) runs without Redis.

# AINDY_AGENT_EXECUTION_BACKEND=nodus_vm
# Agent-execution backend. THIS MONOLITH DEFAULTS TO `nodus_vm` on real boots —
# apps/agent/bootstrap.py::_select_execution_backend() sets it (via setdefault) for
# every non-test deployment; leaving this unset uses nodus_vm. Set it explicitly to
# `agent_flow` to opt back into the runtime's static Python-DAG path. nodus_vm compiles
# each run to a native Nodus workflow executed through the VM; continuation is driven by
# the runtime scheduler heartbeat, which `aindy-runtime serve` starts automatically. RTR-1
# §5 validates it end-to-end (tests/integration/test_nodus_vm.py). The test harness stays
# on `agent_flow` (no scheduler heartbeat there); the §5 suite opts in via pytest.nodus.ini.

# AINDY_AGENT_WAIT_BEFORE_HIGH_RISK=false
# When true (and the backend is nodus_vm), an approval WAIT is inserted before the first
# high-risk step, parking the run at status="waiting" until POST /apps/agent/runs/{id}/resume
# releases it. Default false — nodus_vm runs execute straight through without parking.

# ── Agent PLANNER backend (which engine writes the plan) ──────────────────────
# Distinct from the EXECUTION backend above: the planner decides the steps; the
# execution backend runs them. Enabling the Claude planner is BUILD_PLAN Track 2.

# AINDY_AGENT_PLANNER_BACKEND=runtime_local
# Which engine generates the plan. Default `runtime_local` — a deterministic,
# no-egress planner (used in CI and any environment without model egress). Set to
# `anthropic_chat` to have Claude author a real multi-step, tool-diverse plan. That
# path REQUIRES ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and outbound HTTPS to api.anthropic.com — GitHub-
# hosted runners block this (RTR-1-NODUS-APPTOOL-500), so flip it only in a deploy
# environment with egress (self-hosted runner / cloud box). See docs/deployment/DEPLOYMENT.md.

# AINDY_CLAUDE_PLANNER_MODEL=
# Optional. Overrides the model id the `anthropic_chat` planner requests. Leave
# unset to use the planner's built-in default (a current /v1/messages model;
# planner_anthropic.py already omits the temperature/top_p/budget_tokens params
# that 400 on Opus-class models). Only set this to pin a specific model.


# ── Infinity learned recursion (REFLECT calibration) ──────────────────────────
# Off by default. The learned expected-score model runs only where these are set.
# Soak-then-flip: turn on SHADOW first, confirm the model wins, then ADVISORY.

# AINDY_INFINITY_LEARNED_SHADOW=1
# Phase 0 — trains + logs the learned model alongside the heuristic (shadow); drives
# nothing. Turn on in a running environment to accumulate soak evidence, then read
# `sys.v1.analytics.expectation_shadow_report` (learned vs heuristic MAE + coefficients).

# AINDY_INFINITY_LEARNED_ADVISORY=1
# Phase 1 — blends the learned expectation into the REFLECT accuracy signal (weighted,
# bounded, heuristic-anchored). Flip on only after the shadow soak shows the model wins.
# See docs/architecture/INFINITY_LEARNED_RECURSION_SCOPE.md.


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Group 4 — Local dev overrides
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ENV=development
# AINDY_ALLOW_SQLITE=
# AINDY_SKIP_MONGO_PING=
# SKIP_MONGO_PING=
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO
